and older release URLs not found. Series D 2019 rests on two press-digest stubs on the company site (reported). CONFLICTS/DOUBLE-COUNT WARNINGS: (1) Aug 2025: release says US$22M (C$31M); SEC says Rights Offering US$18.4M (incl. US$1.4M related-party loan settlement) plus CAD 5.0M (~US$3.6M) SIF commitment = ~US$22.0M. The SIF 2026-03-26 amendment event (CAD 5M) is the same money as the SIF part of the US$22M headline; the ledger counts the equity at 18.4M only. (2) SAFEs: SEC gross US$44.5M (Q4 2025 to Jan 2026) vs Globe and Mail via TechCrunch US$51.1M from ~70 investors. (3) Series F: release said US$25M combined first close incl. BC grant; SEC says Class F Series 1 total proceeds US$20.9M (July 2023); announced_on is the release date, closed_on approximated to month-end July 2023. (4) SIF agreement values are authorised maxima (Canada G&C); contributions come with warrants issued to the Crown. The cumulative event is amount_kind=cumulative and must not be summed with increments. SPAC: Spring Valley Acquisition Corp. III IPO (US$230M, 2025-09-05) is the SPAC's own capital, recorded for completeness; trust was heavily redeemed (21,075,896 shares per 20-F pro forma note). The listing event has no amount: company says it entered public markets with approximately US$150M cash inclusive of net private placement and trust proceeds; TechCrunch/FusionX reports US$127M net. PIPE: 10,556,367 units at $10.20 = ~US$107.7M gross vs 'approximately US$105M' in releases; anchor Alyeska inferred from the 20-F beneficial ownership text (8-K only says 'Anchor PIPE Investor'). Nasdaq trading began 2026-07-13 as GFUZ (closing 2026-07-10). Date precision: SAFE announced_on is month-start (Nov 2025); Series D 2019 year from post context. INFUSE and NSERC events carry no amounts; NSERC award is joint with SFU. No ATM programme found. BC grant announced_on is the Series F release date (August 2023, exact day not stated). Reviewer: check new-entity slugs (british-columbia-government, canadian-nuclear-laboratories, tobias-lutke, triumf, renexia, kyoto-fusioneering). VERIFIER 2026-10-05: the CA$20M CNL/BDC lead investment (Aug 2024) is the same money as the July 2024 US$15.8M secured convertible notes (2024 financing inflows were only the notes plus US$1.5M SIF warrants); the notes later converted into Class B Series 2 shares in the Aug 2025 rights offering (non-cash, excluded from the US$18.4M). SPAC trust: 21,075,896 of 23,000,000 SVAC shares were redeemed, so the US$230M SPAC IPO is a ceiling; the residual trust cash reaching General Fusion is not stated in any snapshot (gap). The US$1B pro-forma equity value assumed no redemptions and was removed from valuation_post_usd. INFUSE vouchers fund the national lab (SRNL), not General Fusion. SIF: CAD 74.3M actually received by 2026-06-02 (equal to agreement value), so SIF increments are real money; the prospectus elsewhere says only CAD 3.9M of the final CAD 5.0M had been funded (internal inconsistency).","org":{"aliases":[],"country":"CA","external_ids":{"cik":null,"companies_house":null,"lei":null,"pic":null,"ror":null,"siren":null,"uei":null,"wikidata":null},"hq_city":"Richmond","id":"general-fusion","kind":"company","lat":null,"legal_names":[],"logo":null,"lon":null,"name":"General Fusion","parent_id":null,"website":"https://generalfusion.com"},"totals":{"approx":true,"ceiling":230000000.0,"debt":15800000.0,"disbursed":0.0,"equity":383800000.0,"obligated":0.0,"public":58456131.97,"total":458056131.97,"undisclosed":3}}